diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the OSPF routing process (ospfd) on R6. Mechanism: R7 reaches the rest of the network only via its single OSPF neighbor R6 over link Y (R7.eth0 ↔ R6.eth2). With ospfd down on R6, no OSPF adjacency forms on that link, so R7’s LSAs (its loopbacks 17.x.x.x, its LAN 70.0.0.0/8, and the R6–R7 transit 67.0.0.0/8) are not flooded beyond R7, and R6 also ceases to advertise the 67.0.0.0/8 transit network. As a result, those routes disappear from the rest of the domain, including R1.

